  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a non constant twice differentiable such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>. If a real valued function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>[</mo><mo> </mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></math>, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mq6t9",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for atleast two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "RpgsN",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for exactly one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
